IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Metrication Act 1970 (Singapore) -- what the Act says about the unit a person measures in: whether it is a unit of the
-- International System of Units and in which Schedule (ss 2, 3(2); First, Second and Fourth Schedules), whether using it has
-- legal force (ss 3(1), 7(2)), what a measurement comes to in SI units (s 5, Third Schedule), whether an order converting a
-- written law is one s 4 allows (s 4), and whether something done in another unit can be challenged on that ground alone (s 7(1)).
--
-- SEAT: a person in Singapore who measures, or is given a measurement, in some unit -- a trader, a buyer, a party to a document,
-- anyone subject to a written law that states a quantity. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021; in operation 31 December 2021), as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/MA1970.txt. The only later instrument the deposit records is the rectification G.N. No. S 22/1989
-- of the Fourth Schedule, already incorporated.
--
-- Provisions covered: ss 2, 3, 4, 5, 7; First, Second, Third and Fourth Schedules.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the long title and s 1 (short title); s 6 (the Minister's power to vary the Schedules by Gazette notification --
-- machinery; a later notification would be a new edition, and none is deposited); any order actually made under s 4 (none is
-- deposited, so the date of the order relevant to a person's act is an input). The Act lays no duty on the individual, so there is
-- no regulative rule here.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to
-- whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass,
-- no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Metrication Act 1970 -- the units`

-- The units the Schedules name, plus one the Schedules do not (`foot`), so that the encoding can say what the Act gives a unit it
-- does not list. Each unit's quantity is its plain gloss; it is recorded in the Schedule tables below.
DECLARE Unit IS ONE OF
    -- First Schedule: the 6 basic units
    metre, kilogram, `second`, ampere, kelvin, candela
    -- Second Schedule: the supplementary and derived units
    hertz, newton, joule, watt, coulomb, volt, farad, ohm, weber, tesla, henry, lumen, lux, radian, steradian
    -- Fourth Schedule: units used in conjunction with the others
    hectare, `metric tonne`, litre, `centigrade or Celsius`
    -- Third Schedule: imperial standard units
    yard, pound, gallon
    -- Third Schedule: local customary units
    tahil, kati, chhun, chhek
    -- a unit no Schedule lists
    foot

-- Where a unit sits in the International System of Units (s 3(2)).
DECLARE `SI role` IS ONE OF
    `a basic unit (First Schedule)`
    `a supplementary or derived unit (Second Schedule)`
    `a unit used in conjunction with them (Fourth Schedule)`
    `not a unit of the International System of Units`

-- One row of the First, Second or Fourth Schedule: Unit, Symbol, Quantity, as printed.
DECLARE `Schedule row` HAS
    `unit`     IS A Unit
    `symbol`   IS A STRING
    `quantity` IS A STRING

§§ `First, Second and Fourth Schedules -- as data`

-- First Schedule: "The International System of Units is based on the following 6 basic units:"
`the First Schedule` MEANS
    --                     unit,                     symbol, quantity
    LIST (`Schedule row` OF metre,                    "m",    "length")
       , (`Schedule row` OF kilogram,                 "kg",   "mass")
       , (`Schedule row` OF `second`,                 "s",    "time")
       , (`Schedule row` OF ampere,                   "A",    "electric current")
       , (`Schedule row` OF kelvin,                   "K",    "thermodynamic temperature")
       , (`Schedule row` OF candela,                  "cd",   "luminous intensity")

-- Second Schedule: "The following are the supplementary and derived units of the International System of Units:"
-- The deposited text prints the Quantity column out of step with the Unit column from volt down (farad against "force", ohm against
-- "electric capacitance" ...). The rows below take each quantity in the order printed, so volt ends with "electromotive force" and
-- each later unit takes the next quantity. That realignment is an inference from the layout, not something the text states.
`the Second Schedule` MEANS
    --                     unit,                     symbol, quantity
    LIST (`Schedule row` OF hertz,                    "Hz",   "frequency")
       , (`Schedule row` OF newton,                   "N",    "force")
       , (`Schedule row` OF joule,                    "J",    "work, energy, quantity of heat")
       , (`Schedule row` OF watt,                     "W",    "power")
       , (`Schedule row` OF coulomb,                  "C",    "quantity of electricity, electric charge")
       , (`Schedule row` OF volt,                     "V",    "electric tension, potential difference, electromotive force")
       , (`Schedule row` OF farad,                    "F",    "electric capacitance")
       , (`Schedule row` OF ohm,                      "Ω",    "electric resistance")
       , (`Schedule row` OF weber,                    "Wb",   "flux of magnetic induction, magnetic flux")
       , (`Schedule row` OF tesla,                    "T",    "magnetic flux density, magnetic induction")
       , (`Schedule row` OF henry,                    "H",    "inductance")
       , (`Schedule row` OF lumen,                    "lm",   "luminous flux")
       , (`Schedule row` OF lux,                      "lx",   "illumination")
       , (`Schedule row` OF radian,                   "rad",  "plane angle")
       , (`Schedule row` OF steradian,                "sr",   "solid angle")

-- Fourth Schedule [S 22/89]. The deposited text prints the units in one block and the symbols and quantities in another; the rows
-- pair them in the order printed (an inference from the layout).
`the Fourth Schedule` MEANS
    --                     unit,                     symbol, quantity
    LIST (`Schedule row` OF hectare,                  "ha",   "area")
       , (`Schedule row` OF `metric tonne`,           "t",    "mass")
       , (`Schedule row` OF litre,                    "L",    "volume")
       , (`Schedule row` OF `centigrade or Celsius`,  "°C",   "temperature, temperature interval")

-- The row for a unit in one of the tables, if it is there.
GIVEN u     IS A Unit
      table IS A LIST OF `Schedule row`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Schedule row`
`the row for` u `in` table MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `unit` EQUALS u) table
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST r

GIVEN u     IS A Unit
      table IS A LIST OF `Schedule row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is listed in` u table IF
    CONSIDER `the row for` u `in` table
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST r THEN TRUE

§§ `ss 2 and 3(2) -- is my unit a unit of the International System of Units?`

-- s 2(1): "International System of Units" -- "(a) means the metric system of units as set out in the First and Second Schedules;
-- and (b) includes the units set out in the Fourth Schedule unless there is something in the subject or context thereof
-- inconsistent with such construction or unless it is therein otherwise expressly provided."
-- s 3(2): SI consists of "(a) the basic units set out in the First Schedule; (b) the supplementary and derived units set out in the
-- Second Schedule; and (c) the units which may be used in conjunction with [them] set out in the Fourth Schedule."
--
-- Whether "the subject or context" of the written law the person is reading is inconsistent with counting the Fourth Schedule
-- units, or that law "otherwise expressly provide[s]", is a reading of that other law. It is asked as a fact the person states:
-- `the law I am reading excludes the Fourth Schedule units`.
GIVEN u IS A Unit
      `the law I am reading excludes the Fourth Schedule units` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `SI role`
`What role does my unit play in the International System of Units` u `the law I am reading excludes the Fourth Schedule units` MEANS
    BRANCH
      IF `is listed in` u `the First Schedule`  THEN `a basic unit (First Schedule)`
      IF `is listed in` u `the Second Schedule` THEN `a supplementary or derived unit (Second Schedule)`
      IF `is listed in` u `the Fourth Schedule` AND NOT `the law I am reading excludes the Fourth Schedule units`
                                                THEN `a unit used in conjunction with them (Fourth Schedule)`
      OTHERWISE `not a unit of the International System of Units`

GIVEN u IS A Unit
      `the law I am reading excludes the Fourth Schedule units` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my unit a unit of the International System of Units` u `the law I am reading excludes the Fourth Schedule units` IF
    NOT `What role does my unit play in the International System of Units` u `the law I am reading excludes the Fourth Schedule units`
        EQUALS `not a unit of the International System of Units`

-- The Schedule's Symbol and Quantity for my unit. NOTHING for a unit none of the First, Second or Fourth Schedules lists.
GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A MAYBE `Schedule row`
`the SI Schedule row for` u MEANS
    CONSIDER `the row for` u `in` (append `the First Schedule` (append `the Second Schedule` `the Fourth Schedule`))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST r

GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`What is the symbol of my unit` u MEANS
    CONSIDER `the SI Schedule row for` u
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `symbol`)

GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`What quantity does my unit measure` u MEANS
    CONSIDER `the SI Schedule row for` u
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `quantity`)

-- s 2(2): "The abbreviation 'SI' is recognised as a legal reference to the International System of Units."
-- Unconditional: a document that writes "SI" refers, in law, to the International System of Units.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the abbreviation SI a legal reference to the International System of Units` IF TRUE

§§ `ss 3(1) and 7(2) -- does my use of this unit have legal force?`

-- s 3(1): "On and after 15 February 1971, the use of the system of units known as the International System of Units has legal force
-- and validity in Singapore."
-- s 7(2): "Nothing in this Act affects the legal force and validity of any other system of units lawfully used in Singapore."
--
-- Whether another system of units is "lawfully used" is a question of some other law; the person states it.
-- The Act confers force on SI; it does not take force away from anything else, and it prohibits nothing.
DECLARE `Legal force of my use` IS ONE OF
    `it has legal force and validity under s 3(1)`
    `its force under another lawful system is untouched by this Act (s 7(2))`
    `this Act gives it no legal force`

`the day SI gains legal force` MEANS Date 15 2 1971

GIVEN u IS A Unit
      `the law I am reading excludes the Fourth Schedule units` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I used it` IS A DATE
      `my use is lawful in Singapore under another system of units` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Legal force of my use`
`Does my use of this unit have legal force` u `the law I am reading excludes the Fourth Schedule units` `the day I used it` `my use is lawful in Singapore under another system of units` MEANS
    BRANCH
      IF     `Is my unit a unit of the International System of Units` u `the law I am reading excludes the Fourth Schedule units`
         AND `the day I used it` AT LEAST `the day SI gains legal force`
        THEN `it has legal force and validity under s 3(1)`
      IF `my use is lawful in Singapore under another system of units`
        THEN `its force under another lawful system is untouched by this Act (s 7(2))`
      OTHERWISE `this Act gives it no legal force`

§§ `s 5 and Third Schedule -- what is my measurement in SI units?`

-- s 5: "The values expressed in terms of -- (a) any imperial standard relating to measures of extension whether lineal, superficial
-- or solid, or of weight or capacity; or (b) the local customary system of weights and measures, may be converted into the values
-- expressed in terms of the International System of Units in accordance with the Third Schedule."
-- "may be converted": a permission. The figure is the Third Schedule's; a unit the Schedule does not list has no conversion here.

-- The limb of s 5 a Third Schedule unit falls under.
DECLARE `s 5 limb` IS ONE OF
    `(a) an imperial standard`
    `(b) the local customary system of weights and measures`
    `neither: the Third Schedule does not list this unit`

-- One row of the Third Schedule: 1 unit = value SI unit, "exactly" or "approximately".
DECLARE `Third Schedule row` HAS
    `unit`                  IS A Unit
    `SI value of one unit`  IS A NUMBER
    `SI unit`               IS A STRING
    `exactly`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb`                  IS A `s 5 limb`

-- Third Schedule: "Conversion of Imperial Standard Units to Equivalent SI Units" and "Conversion of Local Customary Units to
-- Equivalent SI Units". The gallon is printed as "= 4.54609 litres approximately = 4.54609 cubic decimetres approximately"; one row
-- carries both names.
`the Third Schedule` MEANS
    --                           unit,    one unit is,  SI unit,                          exactly, limb
    LIST (`Third Schedule row` OF yard,   0.9144,       "metres",                         TRUE,    `(a) an imperial standard`)
       , (`Third Schedule row` OF pound,  0.45359237,   "kilograms",                      TRUE,    `(a) an imperial standard`)
       , (`Third Schedule row` OF gallon, 4.54609,      "litres (or cubic decimetres)",   FALSE,   `(a) an imperial standard`)
       , (`Third Schedule row` OF tahil,  37.799364,    "grams",                          FALSE,   `(b) the local customary system of weights and measures`)
       , (`Third Schedule row` OF kati,   0.604790,     "kilograms",                      FALSE,   `(b) the local customary system of weights and measures`)
       , (`Third Schedule row` OF chhun,  37.465,       "millimetres",                    TRUE,    `(b) the local customary system of weights and measures`)
       , (`Third Schedule row` OF chhek,  0.37465,      "metres",                         TRUE,    `(b) the local customary system of weights and measures`)

GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A MAYBE `Third Schedule row`
`the Third Schedule row for` u MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `unit` EQUALS u) `the Third Schedule`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST r

-- NOTHING means "not covered": the Third Schedule gives no conversion for the unit (an SI unit needs none; a unit like the foot is
-- not listed, and s 5 converts only "in accordance with the Third Schedule").
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      u IS A Unit
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my measurement in SI units` n u MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Third Schedule row for` u
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (n TIMES r's `SI value of one unit`)

GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`In which SI unit is my converted measurement` u MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Third Schedule row for` u
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `SI unit`)

-- JUST TRUE where the Schedule says "exactly", JUST FALSE where it says "approximately", NOTHING where it gives no conversion.
GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the conversion of my unit exact` u MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Third Schedule row for` u
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `exactly`)

GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A `s 5 limb`
`Under which limb of s 5 may my unit be converted` u MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Third Schedule row for` u
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `neither: the Third Schedule does not list this unit`
    WHEN JUST r THEN r's `limb`

§§ `s 4 -- is the order converting my written law one s 4 allows?`

-- s 4(1): "The Minister may by order provide for the adaptation, alteration, conversion or modification of any provisions contained
-- in any written law ... for the purpose of replacing references to units other than metric units contained in the written law
-- with references to units of the International System of Units which are either -- (a) equivalent; or (b) such approximations as
-- appear to the Minister desirable for the purpose of securing that the enactments as adapted, altered, converted or modified are
-- expressed in convenient terms."
-- (2): "Any order made under subsection (1) must be published in the Gazette."
--
-- The provision addresses the Minister. For the person subject to the converted law it answers: is the new figure one the order
-- could lawfully put there? Limb (b) is the Minister's judgment, so it is answered conditionally, as an input: "if the approximation
-- appears to the Minister desirable for convenient terms".
GIVEN `the order replaces a non-metric reference with an SI unit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new figure is equivalent to the old` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approximation appears to the Minister desirable for convenient terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the order converting my written law one s 4 allows` `the order replaces a non-metric reference with an SI unit` `the new figure is equivalent to the old` `the approximation appears to the Minister desirable for convenient terms` `the order was published in the Gazette` IF
        `the order replaces a non-metric reference with an SI unit`
    AND (    `the new figure is equivalent to the old`
         OR  `the approximation appears to the Minister desirable for convenient terms`)
    AND `the order was published in the Gazette`

§§ `s 7(1) -- can what I did be challenged because of the unit I used?`

-- s 7(1): "No act or thing done before the making of any order under section 4 may be challenged only on the ground that the act or
-- thing done was done in a unit other than a unit of the International System of Units."
--
-- Reading taken (a fork the text leaves open): "any order" is read as the s 4 order that touches the written law under which the
-- act was done, and its date is an input. If no such order date is given, the encoding does not say whether the bar applies (read
-- as "before the first order of any kind", or as "every act while no order exists", the text supports more than one answer), and
-- says so with its own constructor.
-- "only on the ground": the bar is to that ground alone. A challenge on any other ground is untouched, and the bar does not apply.
-- "before": an act done on the day the order is made is not done before it.
DECLARE `Challenge on the unit alone` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(1) bars that challenge`
    `s 7(1) does not bar that challenge`
    `not covered by this encoding: no s 4 order date given`

GIVEN `I did it in a unit other than an SI unit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only ground of the challenge is the unit I used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I did it` IS A DATE
      `the day the s 4 order was made` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Challenge on the unit alone`
`Can what I did be challenged only because of the unit I used` `I did it in a unit other than an SI unit` `the only ground of the challenge is the unit I used` `the day I did it` `the day the s 4 order was made` MEANS
    IF NOT (`I did it in a unit other than an SI unit` AND `the only ground of the challenge is the unit I used`)
    THEN `s 7(1) does not bar that challenge`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day the s 4 order was made`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered by this encoding: no s 4 order date given`
         WHEN JUST d THEN IF `the day I did it` LESS THAN d
                          THEN `s 7(1) bars that challenge`
                          ELSE `s 7(1) does not bar that challenge`
